name c01m03-rubicon
timeout 900
time 1994-10-07T06:00:00Z

# ARMORED FIST (NovaLogic 1994), CAMPAIGN ONE "OVERWATCH", MISSION 3 OF 7 — `INDIA3`, RUBICON.
# THE SEVEN DISCLOSURES D1-D7 are stated in full in c01m01-slaughterzone.fbm and apply here unchanged.
#
# THE TASK [FSW]: join ECHO-2, already in contact, and destroy the enemy FIELD COMMAND ENCAMPMENT
# INCLUDING ITS EMPLACED ARTILLERY. Course 220 SSW. Time limit 15 min [FSG].
#
# ECHO-2 IS NAMED BY THE BRIEFING AND HAS NO STRENGTH IN ANY SOURCE. [GUIDE p.61]'s order of battle
# gives one blue row — "Echo 1: 1 M1, 1 M3" — and no Echo-2 row, so this file declares no Echo-2 units.
# THE CONSEQUENCE IS EXPLICIT: the reading rule's clause "Echo-2 losses do not fail the run" has no
# object in the data and is therefore not judged here. Named, not silently dropped.
#
# THE MI-24 HINDS ARE PRESENT AND HARMLESS. [GUIDE p.58-61] warns of "a minimum of two" Hinds. There is
# no rotorcraft in this tree and none was written; the nearest catalogue row is `mi8` (Mi-8MT), a
# KINEMATIC MOVER — no flight model, no stations, no gun, no fire control ([`doc/modules/air/
# catalogue.md`]). So the two Hinds fly their transit and threaten NOTHING. The direction of that error
# is total and one-sided: a Hind's whole purpose is killing armour, and the substitute cannot kill
# anything at all. They are declared anyway, because a threat that is present and impotent is a
# measurement and an absent threat is a gap.
#
# THE MINEFIELDS ARE NOT DECLARED. [FSW] calls the ground "saturated with mine fields and pillboxes"
# and this is the one Overwatch mission whose `STMP` count is ZERO while its briefing mentions mines —
# the single counterexample to the `STMP` = minefield hypothesis (terrain.md §6.2). Nothing in this
# tree is a mine, nothing drives over one, so the declaration would have no reader.
#
# WHAT THIS FILE DECLARES
#   Blue [GUIDE p.61]: Echo 1 = 1 M1A2 + 1 M3. Two vehicles, two jets.
#   Red  [GUIDE p.61]: Bandit 1 (2 T-80, 2 BMP), Bandit 2 (2 T-80). Plus 2 Mi-24.
#   Goals: the ENCAMPMENT and its EMPLACED ARTILLERY, and those two alone — the [FSW] task names no
#   vehicle, and the goal flag that would settle which objects were flagged is in the undecoded `DCBS`
#   (campaign.md §7.4). Neither element carries a count anywhere, so each is declared ONCE and the
#   direction is understated. They sit 150 m apart on the axis of advance, inside ONE CBU-87 footprint
#   by construction (D6) — which is what makes this the campaign's most winnable mission.
#
# READING RULE (binding). The verdict is `m3e1a`'s UNIT_RESULT and nothing else.
#   SUCCESS/exit 0 requires the encampment AND its emplaced artillery destroyed inside 900 s. The
#   Bandit platoons are NOT goals and their survival does not fail the run.
#   exit 3 with either installation INTACT is a delivery failure and is worth reporting as one: both
#   lie under a single canister's declared footprint, so a miss here is the CCRP solution, not the
#   arithmetic.
#   exit 1 on a blue unit is an ENGINE finding, not a mission loss (D2).

unit m3e1a
  module f16
  team friendly
  flight echo1 1
  spawn 26.14740 70.81640 1040 220.0 450      # 40 km short of the encampment on the [FSW] course 220
  set gear up
  set fuel_int_pct 100
  set fcr_mode off
  set rwr on
  set store 3 cbu87
  set brief_master_arm arm
  set task attack
  set attack_mode ccrp
  wp 25.87130 70.55970 1040 450               # AIM POINT: the field command encampment
  wp 25.69874 70.39926 1640 450               # egress 25 km down the axis
  objective kill unit m3camp
  objective kill unit m3arty
  objective survive

unit m3e1b
  module f16
  team friendly
  flight echo1 2
  spawn 26.15609 70.80490 1050 220.0 450      # 1.5 km across track
  set gear up
  set fuel_int_pct 100
  set fcr_mode off
  set rwr on
  set store 3 cbu87
  set brief_master_arm arm
  set task attack
  set attack_mode ccrp
  wp 25.85437 70.55287 1050 450               # AIM POINT: Bandit 1, between Echo and the camp
  wp 25.69874 70.39926 1650 450
  objective survive

# ---- THE OBJECTIVE AREA
unit m3camp
  module target_soft
  team hostile
  spawn 25.87130 70.55970 ground 220.0 0
unit m3arty
  module target_soft
  team hostile
  spawn 25.87026 70.55874 ground 220.0 0      # 150 m down-axis of the encampment

# ---- BANDIT 1 [GUIDE p.61]: 2 T-80, 2 BMP
unit m3b1v1
  module target_hard
  team hostile
  spawn 25.85402 70.55333 ground 220.0 0
unit m3b1v2
  module target_soft
  team hostile
  spawn 25.85425 70.55302 ground 220.0 0
unit m3b1v3
  module target_hard
  team hostile
  spawn 25.85448 70.55272 ground 220.0 0
unit m3b1v4
  module target_soft
  team hostile
  spawn 25.85471 70.55241 ground 220.0 0

# ---- BANDIT 2 [GUIDE p.61]: 2 T-80
unit m3b2v1
  module target_hard
  team hostile
  spawn 25.86217 70.54256 ground 220.0 0
unit m3b2v2
  module target_hard
  team hostile
  spawn 25.86241 70.54225 ground 220.0 0

# ---- THE TWO HINDS [GUIDE]: `mi8` movers, 300 m over the encampment's ground, crossing the objective
unit m3hind1
  module mi8
  team hostile
  spawn 25.87130 70.60962 450 270.0 130
  wp 25.87130 70.50978 450 130
unit m3hind2
  module mi8
  team hostile
  spawn 25.85589 70.60661 450 290.0 130
  wp 25.88671 70.51279 450 130
